{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the son of an Israelite woman went out.</b> From his tent, like יצאו נצבים פתח אהליהם (they stood at the entrance of their tents)." "<b>The son of an Egyptian man.</b> He was a convert [to Judaism]." "<b>And the Israelite man.</b> Like לאיש העשיר את יום השביעי (to the man who completed the seventh day) — but we do not know why this pericope is joined here. Perhaps the matter of the one who cursed is something that should not be, on account of the bread and the oil and the offerings."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:09.535359496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}